            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ereteshka"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My boyfriend turned me on to ham barbecue after I spent my whole life thinking that it was a gross idea. My loss. This is cheap, delicious, and a definite crowd pleaser. It's even better the next day, when everything's thickened up!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Antoinette"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Only used one bottle of chili sauce or it would be too runny",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-22T16:09:57.920Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TxCin2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great barbecue sandwich! Very tangy and a hint of sweet. I scaled this down to 1 serving and it came out with just the right amount of sauce to meat. I added sweet relish to the mix rather than adding it on top. I used shaved mesquite smoked ham. My PA friends relocated here tell me that \"chipped\" ham isn't available here in Texas so I can't say how this would compare to what they are used to, but I thought it was really good and certainly a keeper! Thanks for the great recipe, this is delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-16T12:34:05.510Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As a Pittsburgh-er, I can say that these are really good! The only reason I'm giving it 4 stars instead of 5 is that that is waaaaay too much sauce for only 1 pound of chipped ham. I'm glad that I went w/ my instincts and 1/2'd the sauce part, b/c it would've been a waste of the extra ingredients. Other than that, these were very tasty, had great flavor and I loved the convenience of using the slow cooker...I cooked mine on low for 3 hrs. and that was perfect. I didn't find these too sweet at all, just right! Thanks for sharing this recipe...I WILL be making these again! :)",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-17T16:04:19.533Z"
          },
          {
